 # flightsims
+
 A collection of flight simulators. Open [index.html](./index.html) to choose which simulator to use.
+
+## Skyhawk: pilot checklist and walkaround
+
+Press **Tab** or click **Checklist** to open the pilot's tablet. The tablet tracks Pre-flight, Engine Start, Before Takeoff and Shutdown items. Simulator-observable settings update automatically; transient actions are recorded when observed, and actions the simulator cannot verify require your confirmation. Use **Shift+Tab** for keyboard navigation.
+
+To inspect the exterior, stop on the ground, set the parking brake, shut down the engine, wait for the propeller to stop, and turn the ignition off. Press **7** or choose **Start walkaround** in the tablet. Use **WASD** to walk and drag to look around; select each labeled hotspot, move close enough, and choose **Mark reviewed**. Fuel and landing-gear checklist items require all of their individual stations to be reviewed. Press **1** to return to the cockpit.
+
+For a quick flight, the tablet offers **Skip to ready on runway** while stopped on the ground. After confirmation, it restarts the aircraft on the nearest available runway with the engine running, restores the setup fuel, and resets failures and ATC. A configured start-of-flight failure is disabled for that quick flight; the original restart setup is preserved. The inspection and checklist history are cleared, not certified as completed.
+
+These features are simulator guidance only, not a substitute for an actual aircraft's approved checklist or inspection procedures.
+
+Run the checklist state tests with `node --experimental-default-type=module --test tests/checklist.test.mjs`.
